---
description: Settings and admin forms follow rule 11 of the monorepo's CODING_STANDARDS § Design
globs: ["packages/settings/**", "packages/ui/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

1. A setting is a sentence the owner would say; the control sits where the value goes in the sentence.
2. Every value carries its unit inside the control: a currency symbol in a money field, a time picker for a time.
3. Optional behaviour is a switch, and its value appears when the switch is on. "Leave blank for none" is a bug.
4. The help line says what happens at the till, in one sentence. Never the format, never the label again.
5. Plain words: float, drawer, count, short or over, close. Never variance, threshold, session, expected.
6. The common case is one switch; everything that only matters when it is on is hidden while it is off.
7. Inherited or customised is shown on the field, never implied by blank.
8. Defaults are prefilled and visible in the control, not described in a tip.

The long form with examples: [docs/design/ui-design-guidelines.md, section 11](https://github.com/wcpos/roadmap/blob/main/docs/design/ui-design-guidelines.md) in wcpos/roadmap.
